---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, SOCIAL } from '../consts';

const FACTS = [
	['Experience', '10 years across software engineering, applied AI and product development'],
	['Based in', 'Stuttgart area, Germany'],
	['Education', 'MSc Communication Engineering, Technical University of Munich'],
	['Previously', 'Bosch · Mercedes-Benz Tech Motion'],
	['Now', 'Founder of Anovi · Applied AI systems consultant · Independent product engineer'],
	['Core stack', 'Python · TypeScript · React Native · FastAPI · PostgreSQL'],
	[
		'Focus',
		'Production AI · Mobile and backend systems · Zero-to-one products · Technical investigation',
	],
];
---

<Base
	title="About"
	description="Applied AI systems consultant, product engineer and founder. 10 years across embedded engineering, production AI, mobile and backend systems, and shipped products."
	person
	wide
>
	<section class="hero">
		<div class="hero-copy">
			<p class="eyebrow">About</p>
			<h1>Hi, I'm Pragathi.</h1>
			<p class="sub">
				I have spent the past 10 years building software, intelligent systems and digital products,
				from embedded engineering and applied AI to mobile applications, backend systems and complete
				product releases.
			</p>
			<div class="actions">
				<Button href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`} primary icon="mail">Email</Button>
				<Button href={SOCIAL.linkedin}>LinkedIn</Button>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="hero-visual">
			<span class="halo"></span>
			<img
				class="portrait"
				src="/pragathi.jpg"
				alt="Pragathi Jayaram"
				width="200"
				height="200"
				decoding="async"
			/>
		</div>
	</section>

	<div class="body">
		<div class="prose">
			<p>
				Before working independently, I held engineering roles at Bosch and Mercedes-Benz. My work
				covered computer vision, gaze and pose systems, multimodal AI, explainable AI, transformer and
				speech-based solutions, and the data and evaluation infrastructure underneath them. I studied
				Communication Engineering at TU Munich and completed my thesis on applying AI to radar.
			</p>
			<p>
				Today, I divide my time between building Anovi and taking on selected consulting and
				freelance projects across applied AI, software engineering and product development.
			</p>
			<p>
				I started Anovi because of a gap I kept running into: nutrition advice is often accurate
				and rarely usable. It does not account for what is already in your kitchen, what is
				expiring, what you have time to cook or what you actually enjoy eating. The interesting
				problem was never simply the model. It was translating evidence into a decision someone
				could make on a Tuesday evening.
			</p>
			<p>
				Building Anovi independently meant taking responsibility for the entire product: the
				architecture, database schema, recommendation logic, LLM pipeline, mobile experience,
				payments, localisation, privacy work and release on the App Store and Google Play.
			</p>
			<p>
				That range is why this site exists. Building across disciplines taught me things worth
				documenting, and many of them are not the polished lessons that make it into conference
				talks.
			</p>
			<p>
				What I write here follows one rule: every claim has a receipt. When there is an upstream
				issue, I link to it. When there is not, I show the reproduction, measurement or control that
				supports the conclusion. That includes the approaches I abandoned, the systems that failed
				and the detectors that produced false positives.
			</p>
			<p>
				I write for people who care not only about whether technology works, but why it works,
				where it breaks and what it takes to make it dependable.
			</p>
		</div>

		<aside class="facts-wrap">
			<dl class="facts card">
				{
					FACTS.map(([label, value]) => (
						<div>
							<dt>{label}</dt>
							<dd>{value}</dd>
						</div>
					))
				}
			</dl>
		</aside>
	</div>
</Base>

<style>
	.hero {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 3fr) minmax(0, 2fr);
		gap: 2.5rem;
		align-items: center;
		margin-bottom: 3.5rem;
	}

	.hero h1 {
		font-size: clamp(2rem, 4.5vw, 3rem);
		margin: 0.35rem 0 0.75rem;
	}

	.sub {
		color: var(--muted);
		font-size: var(--step-1);
		max-width: 36rem;
		margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
	}

	.actions {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 0.75rem;
	}

	.hero-visual {
		position: relative;
		display: flex;
		justify-content: center;
		align-items: center;
		min-height: 260px;
	}

	.halo {
		position: absolute;
		width: 260px;
		height: 260px;
		border-radius: 50%;
		background: var(--tint);
	}

	.portrait {
		position: relative;
		width: 200px;
		height: 200px;
		border-radius: 50%;
		object-fit: cover;
		border: 4px solid var(--bg);
		box-shadow: 0 10px 30px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.12);
	}

	.body {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 3fr) minmax(16rem, 2fr);
		gap: 3rem;
		align-items: start;
	}

	.prose {
		font-size: var(--step-0);
	}

	.facts-wrap {
		position: sticky;
		top: 1.5rem;
	}

	.facts {
		margin: 0;
	}

	.facts div {
		padding-block: 0.6rem;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
	}

	.facts div:last-child {
		border-bottom: 0;
		padding-bottom: 0;
	}

	.facts div:first-child {
		padding-top: 0;
	}

	dt {
		font-size: 0.75rem;
		font-weight: 600;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--muted);
		margin-bottom: 0.15rem;
	}

	dd {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: 0.9375rem;
	}

	@media (max-width: 48rem) {
		.hero,
		.body {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}

		.hero-visual {
			order: -1;
			min-height: 200px;
		}

		.halo {
			width: 200px;
			height: 200px;
		}

		.portrait {
			width: 150px;
			height: 150px;
		}

		.facts-wrap {
			position: static;
		}
	}
</style>
